@startuml figure_7-7_oocs_oors_flow
' Figure 7-7 - The OOCS and OORS flow
' Concrete "be46" walkthrough of Table 7-7, grouped into the six phases.

skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam ParticipantPadding 12
skinparam BoxPadding 8
hide footbox

title Figure 7-7 - The OOCS and OORS flow

participant "Data Product's\nSidecar"        as SC
participant "Beth /\nMarketplace"             as MP
participant "ODCS\nContract"                  as DC
participant "DQ Tool\n(JoeThePlumberFixer, Soda, GX, dbt ...)"    as DQ
participant "metaDb"                          as DB
participant "Observability\nPort"             as OP
participant "Juliette /\nMonitoring"          as JM

== 1. Sidecar registers ==
SC ->  MP : 10. Register data product  [OOCS register]
note right of MP: confirmation via Kafka topic
MP --> SC : Ack registration  [OORS]

== 2. Marketplace sends a command ==
MP ->  SC : 20. Request quality check  [OOCS configure]

== 3. Sidecar receives and executes ==
SC ->  DC : 30. Read quality rules  [ODCS]
SC ->  DQ : 31. Delegate checks on Customer.email  [OOCS]
DQ --> SC : 32. Return raw check results  [OORS]

== 4. metaDb stores the results ==
SC ->  DB : 40. Store results  [OORS]

== 5. Sidecar returns the results (optional) ==
note over SC, MP: REST response
SC ->  MP : 50. Completeness: pass (2.1%, threshold 5%)  [OORS]
SC ->  MP : 51. Conformity: fail (14 rows, threshold 0)  [OORS]

== 6. Observability port exposes (on demand) ==
JM ->  OP : 60. Query current state
OP ->  DB : 61. Read latest results
DB --> OP : 62. Return OORS results  [OORS]
OP --> JM : 63. Return current state  [OORS]

@enduml
